$\begin{align}
\left(5^3\right)^{2}&=5^{3\cdot 2}
\\\\
&=5^{6}
\end{align}$

This follows from the general rule $\left(x^m\right)^{n}=x^{m\cdot n}$.

We can also see this is correct by expanding the powers.

$\begin{align}
\left(5^3\right)^{2}&=\underbrace{5^3\cdot 5^3}_\text{2 times}
\\\\\\
&=\underbrace{
\underbrace{5\cdot 5\cdot 5}_\text{3 times}
\cdot \underbrace{5\cdot 5\cdot 5}_\text{3 times}}
_\text{2 times}
\\\\
&=5^{6}
\end{align}$
